Z||000000||mrgone||07-13-2001||04:13 AM||||well i know my starter is going. have known that for a long time. was actually going to pull it out tomorrow.<P>but did that stop me from cruising? no.<P>anyway i get to the bank machine and shut the car off. come back, turn the key pppppppphhhhhb! nothing. i curse and try again ppppbbbb b b b and the lights go dim.<BR>i curse some more and pop the trunk wiggle the wire to the starter and begin to push the car. this is my first ever bump start, ive seen civic dx's do it in less than a 4 foot area so i have no idea how fast i must get this thing going. its rolling a pretty good clip and i jump in, 1st gear, dump clutch phphhhph! nothing. i stop. curse again and then look back with the trunk up, and hit the brakes. my brake lights dont even come on. my battery is dead! oh goody.<P>push the car as fast as i can run hop in, dump clutch and floor the fuc**r. that got it going after a whole bunch of engine movement due to shot mounts. woohoo! no 40$ tow bill.<P>so now i cant shut off my car, so i drive around a bit (which i know is bad for the alternator) and i put the car on ramps in my parking spot. going to yank the battery and the starter hopefully in the morning.<P>just thought id share my 4am experience<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
